@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

QuickSky is a no-bullshit, standalone version control tool built from scratch to fix the stuff that makes version control feel like a chore. No more memorizing convoluted commands, hopping between directories, or fighting legacy workflows.

QuickSky is designed for developers who just want to write code, not fight their tools. It provides native, simplified workflows with no dependency on existing tools like Git.

@section Key Features

@itemize @bullet
@item
One-Click Upload: @code{sky upload} natively handles changes tracking, committing, and remote sync
@item
Repo 0-Hassle Switching: @code{sky change-to <repo-name>} jumps straight to your repo
@item
Pain-Free Rebasing: Rebase by date range or rebase all local changes
@item
Fix Old Commits: Edit past commits without breaking history
@item
Simple Branching: Create/delete/switch branches with built-in logic
@end itemize

@node Installation
@chapter Installation

QuickSky ships with native packages for most platforms.

@section npm Package (Cross-Platform)

For Node.js (v14+) users, install globally:

@example
npm install -g quicksky-cli
@end example

@section DEB Package (Debian/Ubuntu)

Download the latest @file{.deb} from releases and install:

@example
sudo dpkg -i quicksky_1.0.0_amd64.deb
sudo apt-get install -f
@end example

@section macOS Packages

@itemize @bullet
@item
PKG Installer: Download @file{.pkg} and double-click to install
@item
DMG: Drag QuickSky binary to @file{/usr/local/bin}
@end itemize

@section Windows MSI

Download @file{.msi} from releases and run the installer.

@section Verify Installation

Check if working:

@example
sky --help
@end example

@node Quick Start
@chapter Quick Start

@section Initialize Repository

Run in your project directory:

@example
sky init
@end example

Follow prompts for username, remote URL, and main branch name.

@section Basic Workflow

Upload changes:
@example
sky upload "Fix login bug"
@end example

Switch repositories:
@example
sky change-to my-other-project
@end example

Create new branch:
@example
sky branch -a feature/payment
@end example

View commit history:
@example
sky log
@end example

@node Commands
@chapter Commands

@section sky init

Initialize QuickSky repository in current directory.

Prompts for:
@itemize @bullet
@item Username (for commit attribution)
@item Remote repository URL
@item Main branch name
@end itemize

@section sky upload [MESSAGE]

Commit and push changes to remote repository.

If no message provided, auto-generates timestamped commit message.

Examples:
@example
sky upload "Fix login bug"
sky upload
@end example

@section sky log

View all commit records in reverse chronological order.

Shows SHA, author, timestamp, message, and file changes.

@section sky branch [OPTIONS] [NAME]

Branch management operations:

@table @code
@item -a NAME
Create and switch to new branch
@item -d NAME
Delete branch (cannot delete current branch)
@item NAME
Switch to existing branch
@item (no args)
List all branches and show current branch
@end table

Examples:
@example
sky branch -a feature/payment
sky branch main
sky branch -d old-feature
sky branch
@end example

@section sky change-to REPO-NAME

Switch to different repository by name.

QuickSky maintains a global registry of repositories.

Example:
@example
sky change-to my-other-project
@end example

@section sky rebase [OPTIONS] [RANGE]

Rebase commits with various options:

@table @code
@item --all
Rebase all local changes
@item YYYY-MM-DD -> YYYY-MM-DD
Rebase commits within date range
@item fuck-base
Undo last rebase operation
@end table

Examples:
@example
sky rebase --all
sky rebase 2024-10-01 -> 2024-10-05
sky rebase fuck-base
@end example

@section sky reload COMMIT-SHA NEW-MESSAGE

Edit past commit message by SHA without breaking history.

Example:
@example
sky reload a1b2c3d "Correct function name (fixes #42)"
@end example

@node Configuration
@chapter Configuration

@section Repository Configuration

@table @file
@item .quicksky/config.toml
Repository configuration file containing user, remote, and branch settings
@end table

@section Commit Storage

@table @file
@item .quicksky/commits/
Directory containing binary-serialized commit records
@item .quicksky/branches.json
Branch state tracking file
@item .quicksky/last_files.json
File hash cache for change detection
@end table

@section Global Registry

@table @file
@item ~/.quicksky_registry.json
Global repository registry for repo switching
@end table

@section Ignore Rules

@table @file
@item .skyhide
QuickSky-specific ignore rules (takes precedence over .gitignore)
@item .gitignore
Standard ignore rules (supported for compatibility)
@end table

@node Examples
@chapter Examples

@section Basic Workflow

Initialize repository:
@example
sky init
@end example

Make changes and upload:
@example
sky upload "Add new feature"
@end example

View history:
@example
sky log
@end example

@section Branch Management

Create feature branch:
@example
sky branch -a feature/login
@end example

Work on feature and upload:
@example
sky upload "Implement login form"
@end example

Switch back to main:
@example
sky branch main
@end example

Delete feature branch:
@example
sky branch -d feature/login
@end example

@section Repository Switching

Switch to different project:
@example
sky change-to my-api-project
@end example

Work and upload:
@example
sky upload "Fix API endpoint"
@end example

Switch back:
@example
sky change-to my-frontend-project
@end example

@section Advanced Operations

Rebase all changes:
@example
sky rebase --all
@end example

Rebase specific date range:
@example
sky rebase 2024-01-01 -> 2024-01-31
@end example

Fix old commit message:
@example
sky reload abc123 "Better commit message"
@end example

Undo rebase if needed:
@example
sky rebase fuck-base
@end example

@node Troubleshooting
@chapter Troubleshooting

@section Common Issues

@table @asis
@item Repository not initialized
Run @code{sky init} in your project directory
@item No changes detected
Ensure files are not ignored by @file{.skyhide} or @file{.gitignore}
@item Branch doesn't exist
Use @code{sky branch} to list available branches
@item Repository not found
Repository may not be registered. Re-run @code{sky init} or check @file{~/.quicksky_registry.json}
@end table

@section Getting Help

Command help:
@example
sky --help
sky COMMAND --help
@end example

Report bugs:
@example
https://github.com/Saladin5101/QuickSky/issues
@end example

@section File Locations

Check these files for debugging:
@itemize @bullet
@item @file{.quicksky/config.toml} - Repository config
@item @file{~/.quicksky_registry.json} - Global registry
@item @file{.quicksky/branches.json} - Branch state
@end itemize

@bye